# Network & System Health API

A containerized FastAPI backend service designed to expose system and network health metrics, built with production-grade containerization and Kubernetes deployment in mind.

This project demonstrates hands-on experience with Docker, Kubernetes, autoscaling (HPA), health probes, and cluster-level troubleshooting.

---

## 🚀 Key Capabilities

- RESTful health monitoring API
- CPU, memory, and disk usage metrics
- Network diagnostics (hostname & IP)
- Dockerized deployment
- Kubernetes-ready manifests
- Liveness & readiness probes
- Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA) based on CPU usage
- Metrics Server integration
- InitContainers for controlled startup workflows

---

## 🧱 Architecture Overview

FastAPI → Docker → Kubernetes Deployment → Service → HPA → Metrics Server

Designed to simulate real-world containerized infrastructure environments.

---

## 🧰 Tech Stack

- Python 3.11
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn
- Docker
- Kubernetes
- Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)
- Linux

